Subject: zink: reclaim freed slab entries and cached buffers while the client is idle

zink only reclaims slab entries and expired cached buffers during its next
allocation. A client that frees a lot and then goes idle keeps all of it
allocated: Steam's web helper held 500-700 MiB of KGSL memory behind a
fullscreen game after scrolling its library, and released it the moment the
overlay drew a frame. A thread now reclaims once a second after a second
without allocations.

